326 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (During the six rounds simulation, the industry competition eventually differentiated two logics of market segmentation, one is innovation-based market segments like High-End, Performance, and Size, which depend on the precision of the product position and its revision timing. But the other type of market segments like Traditional, and Low-End that depend on price and supply stability. Therefore, the competition in the later stage is no longer merely about the product itself but about who can establish a combination of capabilities that best match the selected market. This trend also led to the gradual differentiation of major competitors. Andrews has demonstrated a stronger first-mover advantage and positioning in the innovation-driven niche market, thereby establishing itself as the most important competitive benchmark. Ferris and Baldwin have maintained a relatively wide market presence. In contrast, although Chester chose a niche differentiation path that prioritises High-End, with Performance and Size as secondary, he was more of a fast follower later on. Rather than a true niche leader. In other words, Chester did not fail to enter attractive niche markets, but failed to establish a strong enough positioning, timing, and cost discipline in these markets, thus making it difficult to transform niche participation into a sustainable competitive advantage.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
