/P 126 0 R
/E (As Figure 3.4.1 shows, sales of Cure rose from 344 to 468 between R3 and R4, whilst inventory fell sharply from 148 to 2 \(shown in Figure 3.4.2\), and the contribution margin increased from 27% to 30%, indicating that the company has identified and preliminarily validated a genuine opportunity in this segment. Meanwhile, the Agape of Andrews increased from 1,093 to 1,382 with 39% to 45% in the margin, suggesting that the company pursued the opportunity earlier, and it more effectively and faster managed to leverage its competitive advantage for market leadership. Consequently, the figures do not suggest that Chester lacks strategic direction. Rather than that, they show that although the company has identified a viable growth avenue, it still lacks the capacity to rapidly translate product improvements into market leadership and to execute synergistically.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [37]
