658 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 138 0 R
/E (6.2.2 Differentiation without cost discipline is fragile)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
659 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 138 0 R
/E (The second lesson we learned is the importance of aligning cost discipline with our niche differentiation strategies. It is evident that although our intended strategy is to compete in high-end innovative markets, we failed to invest adequately in each product. For instance, the automation level for cake in the traditional segment remained at 5.0 in round 5, resulting in uncompetitive labour costs and further increasing our COGS \(cost of goods sold\); hence, our contribution margin remains low across six rounds of simulations. Additionally, on the operational decisions, we aggressively invested in promo and sales budget in the marketing department without considering the R&D positioning in round 3, further driving us to fail in generating the necessary sales volume to dilute our high fixed marketing expenses; therefore, our SG&A results remain higher than those of other competitors.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
660 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 138 0 R
/E (6.2.3 High-End success depends on timing, not simply participation)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
