/P 139 0 R
/E (6.3 What the Team Would Do Differently if Renewed)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
675 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (If renewed, Chester will transform from an ambitious niche expansion to a capital-efficient execution based on the following strategies.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
676 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (6.3.1 Strategic Portfolio Optimisation)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
677 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (Chester will transition to a highly focused product portfolio rather than investing broadly across segments to avoid getting stuck in the middle, ensuring that the niche differentiation strategy aligns with real execution. Specifically, we will concentrate our capital on fewer, clearer niches where we can leverage timing and performance advantages to gain sustainable competitive advantages without overextending our support segments.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
678 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (6.3.2 Capital Reallocation)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
679 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (Given that the target of the renewal is to achieve capital-efficient execution, in which the reallocation of capital is necessary during the process. Chester will restructure the investment in automation into the early phase to secure the structural cost advantages and fund more in our high-end innovations. Beyond that, we will also consider investing more in TQM in the lifecycle to reduce material costs and shorten the R&D cycle, ensuring our products can be launched to market as soon as possible, thereby further reducing SG&A burdens and improving the niche differentiation strategy.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
