694 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (In conclusion, Chester demonstrated unsustainable strategies across six rounds of simulations, in which the actual investment decisions were misaligned with the intended strategies and plans. During the early phase of the simulations, we experienced severe forecasting errors and delayed automation in the production department, creating a negative path dependency that ultimately led to an irreparable liquidity crisis in round 3. Although we made some small improvements in the later rounds, those defensive actions came too late to counter industry leaders such as Andrew, who secured sustainable competitive advantages from round 2 in its product positioning and cost-efficient executions. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
695 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (Moving forward, Chester will transition from unfocused expansion to capital-efficient investment decisions by executing strategic portfolio optimisation, prioritising automation in the early phase when new products launch, and ensuring that all decisions are made in line with our forecasting protocols. In other words, Chester will reposition in the market through rebuilding structural cost advantages and capturing sustainable value in the target niche markets. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
